    "model_design": "Add one learned, bias-free hidden_units-to-hidden_units output projection to NextItNetModel, introducing 4,096 parameters at width 64 so sequence representations can adapt their matching geometry while retaining tied item embeddings. Register self.output_proj = nn.Linear(hidden_units, hidden_units, bias=False) after existing backbone and embedding initialization, then initialize its weight with nn.init.eye_ under torch.no_grad(), preserving the initial scoring function for identical backbone parameters without disturbing their initialization order. Replace encode_sequence's final return with self.output_proj(self.norm(x)) * mask so forward and score_candidates share the projected representation, padding remains zero, and all existing variable names, method signatures, candidate-handling behavior, and output shapes are preserved. Keep the current position-free gated local/dilated convolutions, eight independent blocks, dilation schedule, learned residual scales, normalization, dropout, embeddings, and all eight constants unchanged, including WEIGHT_DECAY=0.00001; retain exactly the permitted imports and two classes with methods only. Allocate one of the 44 candidate slots for the unchanged seed-2024 host to compare validation HR@10 against 0.665 using its existing splits, sampled candidates, training, and checkpoint selection, retaining the change only on measured improvement and adding no test-metric access, model-side training, evaluation, printing, file/network access, or submission generation.",
    "training_evaluation": null
  }
